digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56611-5
  rankdir="TB";
  "N1" [label="(2,0,0) Da Vinci documented that rising bubbles spontaneously abandon straight paths for helical trajectories, a paradox persisting for centuries."];
  "N10" [label="(11,0,0) Jellyfish and other marine invertebrates deform their bodies to swim without vortex shedding, leveraging inertial fluid forces."];
  "N12" [label="(0,0,0) If organisms can leverage inertial forces through body deformation for propulsion without viscous traction, then similar mechanisms might apply to other deformable objects in fluids."];
  "N14" [label="(21,0,0) Actuated-bubble technologies have been developed for various purposes across numerous fields."];
  "N15" [label="(22,0,0) In medicine, bubbles are used for manipulating cell properties and for drug and gene delivery."];
  "N16" [label="(23,0,0) Bubbles are exploited as cleaning tools to treat wastewater, prevent biofouling, and clear bacteria from narrow conduits."];
  "N17" [label="(24,0,0) Manipulating bubble motion is valuable in boiling-based heat transfer for cooling electronic microdevices, where unremoved bubbles reduce heat transfer efficiency."];
  "N18" [label="(25,0,0) In micro-gravity settings such as satellites and spacecrafts, the absence of buoyancy complicates bubble evacuation."];
  "N19" [label="(0,0,0) If bubbles are already utilized across diverse technological fields but face control challenges, then improved bubble manipulation methods would have broad technological impact."];
  "N2" [label="(3,0,0) When exposed to acoustic excitations, bubbles transition from in-place pulsations to dancing along zigzag paths reminiscent of Brownian motion."];
  "N20" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Bubbles are applied in medicine, wastewater treatment, biofouling prevention, bacterial cleaning, and heat transfer management, with challenges in micro-gravity. Given that bubbles are utilized across diverse fields but face control challenges, therefore improved methods for controlling bubble dynamics would enable enhanced applications across multiple technological domains."];
  "N21" [label="(20,0,0) Given the multifaceted physics of bubbles, harnessing their dynamics may be challenging but holds significant potential rewards."];
  "N22" [label="(0,0,0) If bubble dynamics are complex but hold potential rewards, and if improved control methods are needed across applications, then discovering new bubble control mechanisms would address both scientific and technological needs."];
  "N24" [label="(9,0,0) A bubble inside a vertically vibrated fluid chamber may spontaneously break symmetry and start to gallop along the upper wall, self-propelled through resonant interaction between its vibration modes."];
  "N25" [label="(10,0,0) By adjusting vibrational forcing, galloping bubbles can be tuned to transition between different domain exploration modes including rectilinear, orbital, and run-and-tumble motion."];
  "N28" [label="(0,0,0) If bubble motion can be tuned by adjusting vibrational forcing to produce different exploration modes, then this provides a controllable mechanism for directing bubble behavior."];
  "N29" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction: Galloping bubbles transition between rectilinear, orbital, and run-and-tumble motion by adjusting vibrational forcing. Given that bubble motion can be tuned by adjusting vibrational forcing, therefore vibrational forcing provides a tunable control mechanism for directing bubble motion and exploration patterns."];
  "N3" [label="(6,0,0) In vertically oscillating baths, bubbles may overcome buoyancy and sink, contradicting common intuition and appearing to violate Archimedes' principle."];
  "N30" [label="(0,0,0) If a phenomenon provides both mechanistic understanding and tunable control, then it enables systematic manipulation."];
  "N33" [label="(0,0,0) If a novel bubble control mechanism addresses existing technological needs and enables new capabilities, then it constitutes a valuable research contribution with broad applications."];
  "N4" [label="(4,0,0) Under sudden pressure changes, bubbles swiftly collapse, giving rise to shock waves that cause cavitation damage to machinery."];
  "N5" [label="(5,0,0) In some instances, bubble implosion becomes so intense that bubbles emit sparks of light (sonoluminescence)."];
  "N6" [label="(7,0,0) Waves of bubbles surge downwards in carbonated drinks, resulting from convection currents in the core of the glass."];
  "N7" [label="(8,0,0) Fascinating bubble dynamics span diverse settings including soft and biological matter, geophysical flows, and industrial processes."];
  "N8" [label="(0,0,0) If multiple independent observations show bubbles exhibiting autonomous, counterintuitive behaviors across different conditions, then bubbles possess inherent complex dynamics that appear to have a life of their own."];
  "N9" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Bubbles exhibit diverse complex behaviors including helical motion, acoustic-induced zigzag paths, sinking in oscillating baths, violent collapse, light emission, and downward waves in drinks. Given these multiple independent observations of autonomous counterintuitive behaviors, therefore bubbles possess inherent complex dynamics and appear to behave autonomously with counterintuitive properties."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes and evaluates galloping bubbles in vertically vibrated liquids as a resonance-based, inertia-powered, tunable self-propulsion mechanism for understanding complex bubble dynamics and developing controllable methods to transport, sort, remove, navigate, and clean with bubbles.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When a physical system exhibits rich autonomous dynamics and a specific controllable mechanism is shown to enable useful manipulation capabilities, those conclusions jointly motivate a research program to understand and exploit that mechanism."];
  "R4" [label="(0,0,0) Because marine invertebrates can swim by deforming their bodies and leveraging inertial fluid forces, analogous inertial propulsion mechanisms may be considered for other deformable objects in fluids."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) The combination of challenging but potentially rewarding bubble dynamics and broad technological needs for improved bubble manipulation motivates discovering new bubble control mechanisms."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) A bubble that gallops along the upper wall of a vertically vibrated fluid chamber through resonant interaction between vibration modes is plausibly an example of self-propulsion by deformable-body inertial mechanisms."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) Because galloping bubbles have a plausible resonant inertial self-propulsion mechanism and their motion modes can be tuned by vibrational forcing, the phenomenon supports systematic manipulation of bubble behavior."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Galloping-bubble dynamics constitute a valuable research contribution because they connect a motivated need for new bubble control mechanisms with systematic manipulation and proof-of-concept capabilities such as tunable size production, bubble sorting and removal, fluid-network navigation, and surface cleaning."];
  "N1" -> "N9" [label="induction-case"];
